The Kernel class is sealed and has a public constructor that takes an IServiceProvider and an optional KernelPluginCollection. It exposes a LoggerFactory property indirectly via the Services property (I need to confirm this). To test the logging behavior in the extension methods, I can create a real Kernel instance by passing a mock IServiceProvider that returns a mock ILoggerFactory when requested.

I will create a mock IServiceProvider that returns a mock ILoggerFactory, which in turn returns a mock ILogger. This will allow the extension methods to call the logger and I can verify the LogTrace call.

